foundationdb 7.3.81: build against OpenSSL 4.x

OpenSSL 4.0 const-qualified the X509 accessors (X509_get_subject_name(),
X509_get_issuer_name(), X509_NAME_get_entry(), X509_NAME_ENTRY_get_data())
and made ASN1_STRING opaque. FDB 7.3 breaks in four places:

  1. flow/MkCert.cpp makeCertNative() added entries to the pointer
     X509_get_subject_name() returns, which is now const. It now builds a
     fresh X509_NAME and installs a copy with X509_set_subject_name(); the
     encoded certificate is the same. MkCert only generates test/tool certs.
  2. flow/TLSConfig.actor.cpp match_criteria_entry()/match_name_criteria():
     const X509_NAME_ENTRY / ASN1_STRING. Type qualifiers only.
  3. flow/TLSConfig.actor.cpp check_verify()/match_criteria(): const
     X509_NAME for the subject/issuer. Type qualifiers only; no comparison,
     branch or return value changes in the peer-verification rules.
  4. The bundled Boost 1.78 asio rfc2818_verification.ipp reads ASN1_STRING
     members directly. Not patched here: build.sh pre-defines its include
     guard (FDB never uses that deprecated class; Boost >= 1.87 removed it).

Source-compatible with OpenSSL 3.x. Not upstream: apple/foundationdb#14348
pins OpenSSL 3.5 instead. Drop this patch when upstream supports OpenSSL 4.

